hai bien khong can

Why the control could send: the probe transport mirrors apps/api/src/common/mail/mail.service.ts
(host, port, secure, auth; no forceAuth), and nodemailer sends AUTH only when the server advertises
it (node_modules/nodemailer/lib/smtp-transport/index.js:260, connection.allowsAuth || options.forceAuth).
The container logs show the difference:
$ docker logs ats-sp3-mailpit-probe
  ... level=info msg="[smtpd] enabling any authentication (insecure)"
  ... level=info msg="[smtpd] starting on [::]:1025 (no encryption)"
$ docker logs ats-sp3-mailpit-control
  ... level=info msg="[smtpd] starting on [::]:1025 (no encryption)"   (no authentication line)
So without the variables Mailpit does not advertise AUTH and the API transport skips AUTH and sends.
Per the plan this is not a stop condition; the two variables stay in docker-compose.test.yml (Task 9).
Not observed directly: that AUTH was actually exchanged in the Step 4a run (Mailpit's log does not
record per-session AUTH); only that the AUTH-enabled server accepted the API-shaped transport.

